From 0a459c65afbcb28f9861134588f9daa1795c1bb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: konnect-patch <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:01:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add KiCad-native Specctra round trip through the ActionPlugin
 bridge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Konnect's own Specctra exporter deliberately supports a narrow profile
(circle/rect pads, straight outline, no NPTH), so most real boards —
every KiCad standard SMD passive uses rounded-rectangle pads — cannot be
exported, and the strict SES importer only accepts sessions routed from
that exporter's DSN.

Add two tools that delegate the geometry to KiCad itself:

- export_specctra_dsn_native (pcb_export): KiCad's own DSN via the
  authenticated ActionPlugin bridge, plus a manifest binding the DSN to
  the SHA-256 of the exact live IPC board snapshot.
- import_specctra_ses_native (pcb_routing): refuses unless the live board
  is byte-identical to the exported revision, then asks the plugin to run
  pcbnew.ImportSpecctraSES (File > Import > Specctra Session) on the
  active board, leaving it modified and unsaved.

The plugin gains a POST /v1/import-specctra-ses operation; the status
response is unchanged so older Rust clients keep working, and a plugin
without the operation is reported as needing an update (404).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
